        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Michelangelo</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1475 CE – 1564 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">6 March 1475 in Caprese, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arezzo">Arezzo</a>, Tuscany, as Michelangelo di Lodovico Buonarroti Simoni; son of Ludovico, then the town's judicial administrator, from a Florentine family of small-scale bankers, and Francesca di Neri del Miniato di Siena</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">18 February 1564 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, aged 88; his body was taken to the Basilica of Santa Croce in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, as he had asked, after a state funeral organised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici">Cosimo I de' Medici</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Sculptor, painter, architect and poet; architect of St Peter's Basilica from 1546</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the Pietà (St Peter's Basilica); the statue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> (1504); the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistine-chapel-ceiling">Sistine Chapel ceiling</a> (1508–1512) and The Last Judgment (1534–1541); the Medici Chapel and the Laurentian Library; the tomb of Julius II, with its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moses">Moses</a>; the design of the dome of St Peter's; more than three hundred sonnets and madrigals</span></div>
